<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{{ .Title }} | {{ .AppName }}</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/styles.css?v=20260905-1"></head>
<body class="public-page"><header class="public-nav"><a class="brand" href="/">{{ .AppName }}</a><nav><a href="/freelancers">Find freelancers</a><a href="/find-jobs">Find jobs</a><a href="/dashboard">My profile</a></nav></header>
<main class="legal-page" style="max-width:840px;margin:40px auto;padding:24px;line-height:1.8">
<h1>Marketplace privacy & payment terms</h1><p>Effective version: {{ .Version }}</p>
<p>This notice supplements our <a href="/legal/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> and <a href="/legal/terms-of-service">terms of service</a> for people hiring or providing freelance services on {{ .AppName }}. The platform operator identified in those terms is responsible for marketplace information. Contact the platform owner through <a href="/chat">platform support</a> for privacy requests or payment questions.</p>
<h2>Your profile and public display</h2><p>We collect your display name, professional title, biography, profile photo, skills (including custom skills), city or region and country. We also calculate availability from active jobs and record completed and published job counts, employer ratings and reviews.</p>
<p>When you choose to publish your profile and check the public-display agreement, you allow {{ .AppName }} to display that photo and those profile details across its pages, including the homepage, freelancer directory, profile pages, job pages and talent recommendations. This permission is for presenting your services and operating the marketplace. It does not grant employers ownership of your photo or authorize unrelated third-party advertising.</p>
<p>Public pages can be seen by any visitor and may be indexed by search engines. Do not put your street address, ID number, private contact details or other sensitive information into public profile fields, proposals, job descriptions or reviews. You can keep a private profile draft. To withdraw public-display consent, uncheck “Publish my profile” on your dashboard and save. Your profile will leave the public directory; third-party caches may take time to update. Existing contracts, proposals, public job records and payment records may remain to operate contracts and resolve disputes. You can request correction or removal through support.</p>
<h2>Private identity information</h2><p>We collect a government-issued ID image for identity review, future validation, fraud prevention and payout verification. It is stored separately from public uploads. Only you and authorized platform owner administrators can retrieve it; employers and visitors cannot view it. We do not publish ID images or use them for advertising. An uploaded image is marked pending until reviewed; submitting an image alone does not mean you are verified.</p>
<p>You can remove an ID image from your dashboard. Removal clears your verification status and may prevent new applications, hires or withdrawals until you submit a new image and, for withdrawal, obtain approval. Identity images are retained while you maintain verification, unless removed by you or the operator. Account deletion removes the stored ID and profile; unresolved work or money must first be settled. The operator may retain records required for disputes or legal obligations under the main privacy policy.</p>
<h2>Jobs, proposals and account activity</h2><p>We use job descriptions, budgets, offers, proposal messages, work submissions, reviews, Connect balances and payment records to match people, form and perform contracts, prevent duplicate or abusive bids, handle payments and resolve disputes. Employers can see proposals for their own jobs; freelancers can see their own proposals. Work submission details are visible to the employer and hired freelancer. Open job descriptions and budgets are public.</p>
<p>Basic freelancing and hiring do not require a monthly subscription. Premium subscriptions and the 14-day trial apply to bug reporting. The current allowance is {{ .ConnectsAmount }} free Connects {{ if eq .ConnectsPeriod "monthly" }}on the first day of each month{{ else }}each Monday{{ end }} at 00:00 UTC. The platform owner can change the allowance and reset schedule; existing balances change at the next scheduled reset. Manual grants are added to your balance and expire at that reset. Unused Connects do not accumulate. Each bid costs 10 Connects, with one proposal per job. Accepting an invitation does not cost Connects. Bids do not guarantee hiring; used Connects are not restored if you are not selected or a job is cancelled.</p>
<h2>Top-ups, hiring and refunds</h2><p>Employers must fund their wallet before publishing and have enough available balance to hire. Payments use USD. A PayPal top-up is credited only after a completed payment is verified. On hiring, the agreed price moves from available hiring balance to reserved job funds. The employer makes the final selection after a bid or accepted invitation. Unselected offers do not reserve funds.</p>
<p>Unused, unreserved hiring balance is refundable on request, subject to verification and actual provider transaction costs. Those costs may reduce the refunded amount. Refunds are returned to the original payment method, after the platform owner checks the original transaction. Money reserved for ongoing work cannot be requested as an unused-balance refund. Contact support about disputes or cancellation after hiring.</p>
<h2>Commission, approval and withdrawals</h2><p>The platform deducts a 5% commission from each employer-approved job payment, rounded to the nearest cent. The freelancer receives the remaining 95%. For example, a $100 approved payment produces a $5 platform fee and $95 in freelancer earnings before any withdrawal transaction costs.</p>
<p>Earnings are held for seven full days from employer approval before becoming available for withdrawal. Withdrawals require approved identity verification. Requested withdrawals are removed from available earnings while awaiting settlement; a rejected request restores the amount. Actual payout transaction costs are deducted from the requested amount and recorded in payment history. There is no additional 5% fee at withdrawal.</p>
<p>Refunds and withdrawals are processed through an owner settlement queue. “Requested” means queued, not paid. “Paid” means the owner has recorded an external payment reference. Processing after the seven-day hold depends on owner review and the payment provider; the hold is not a promise of same-day delivery. Contact support about a disputed payment.</p>
<h2>Service providers, retention and your choices</h2><p>Payment providers receive information needed to process checkout and settlement under their own privacy terms. Hosting, database and email providers may process information to operate the platform. The platform does not receive your full card details through PayPal checkout. Provider locations and international processing are governed by the main privacy policy and the providers' terms.</p>
<p>Public profile display relies on your recorded permission. Contract and transaction processing supports the services you request; verification and abuse prevention protect the marketplace, subject to applicable law. Consent records include the policy version and the time you publish or withdraw. We keep contract, transaction and consent records as needed to operate accounts, reconcile money, resolve disputes and meet applicable recordkeeping obligations. Contact support for the retention rules applicable to your account.</p>
<p>You can edit profile details and withdraw public-display permission in your dashboard. Contact support to request access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection or a copy of your information, where applicable. You may also contact your local data protection authority. Withdrawing consent does not undo processing already performed. We will explain material changes before seeking consent to a new public-display purpose.</p>
</main><footer class="public-footer compact"><span>&copy; {{ .Year }} {{ .AppName }}</span><a href="/legal/privacy-policy">General privacy policy</a><a href="/dashboard">Manage my profile</a></footer></body></html>
